     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>The source of the files is explained in the document: <a href=\"ftp://ftp.jax.org/MUGA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">ftp://ftp.jax.org/MUGA</a></div><div>I believe the physical positions are mm10, but I&#39;m not positive.</div><div><br></div><div>The readme file there says <br></div><div>&quot;Thanks to Andrew Morgan of UNC for providing the marker locations at:&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.muga.Rdata\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.muga.Rdata&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw11mgAvi641PyYv0FTLeD0s\">http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.muga.Rdata</a><br><a href=\"http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.megamuga.Rdata\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.megamuga.Rdata&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3T9W3bEvbyZaCnmzInXXZ0\">http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.megamuga.Rdata</a><br><a href=\"http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.gigamuga.Rdata\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.gigamuga.Rdata&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ju_bSDwtXEwt1BdNqz-uH\">http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/snps.gigamuga.Rdata</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you go to <a href=\"http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Skhm2zrwgRveoPEdbJSYB\">http://csbio.unc.edu/MUGA/</a> there&#39;s a table that suggests that the muga and megamuga locations are in mm9 and the gigamuga locations are mm10.<br></div><div><br></div><div>karl<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wednesday, November 4, 2020 at 7:08:29 PM UTC-6 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">katz...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">... in relation to some old results. </div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Nov 4, 2020 at 3:17 PM Karl Broman &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">kbr...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>I&#39;d recommend using the maps from here: <a href=\"https://github.com/kbroman/MUGAarrays\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kbroman/MUGAarrays&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nVK32wlFw0AUHeL0j2ay8\">https://github.com/kbroman/MUGAarrays</a></div><div>Positions in mm10.</div><div><br></div><div>karl<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wednesday, November 4, 2020 at 1:44:03 PM UTC-6 <a rel=\"nofollow\">katz...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">I&#39;d like to confirm something I&#39;ve always assumed. The map positions for the DO genotype files linked to at <a href=\"https://kbroman.org/qtl2/pages/prep_do_data.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kbroman.org/qtl2/pages/prep_do_data.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Y2IKs-dB85PH8aN8xwEr_\">https://kbroman.org/qtl2/pages/prep_do_data.html</a> are, and have been since that web page went up, grcm38 (mm10). Right?</blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R/qtl2 discussion&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">rqtl2-disc+...@googlegroups.com</a>.</blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/rqtl2-disc/c5b65431-b75d-45f0-8b69-03f760dba2ffn%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/rqtl2-disc/c5b65431-b75d-45f0-8b69-03f760dba2ffn%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483697508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1actobNu_LdPaDTp7AUWwz\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/rqtl2-disc/c5b65431-b75d-45f0-8b69-03f760dba2ffn%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">David C. Katz, Ph.D.<br><div style=\"font-size:12.